ANSER: {
  "scope": "ISO 45001 clause 6.1 (Actions to address risks and opportunities) at a mining operation with underground and surface activities, covering 800 workers across 3 shifts, permit-to-work systems, and addressing the context of 2 lost-time injuries in the past quarter.",
  "criteria": "ISO 45001:2018 standard, specifically clause 6.1 (Actions to address risks and opportunities), including 6.1.1 (General), 6.1.2 (Hazard identification), 6.1.3 (Assessment of OH&S risks), and 6.1.4 (Assessment of OH&S opportunities). Additional criteria include the organization's internal OH&S policies, procedures, and legal requirements applicable to mining operations.",
  "schedule": "The audit will be conducted over 5 days, with the first day dedicated to planning and document review, followed by 3 days of on-site inspections and interviews across all shifts (underground and surface), and the final day for reporting and closing meetings. The audit will be scheduled within the next 4 weeks to ensure timely follow-up on the recent lost-time injuries.",
  "resource_needs": "Audit team of 3 qualified auditors with experience in mining and ISO 45001, including one lead auditor. Access to relevant documents (risk assessments, incident reports, permit-to-work records), PPE for underground visits, and coordination with shift supervisors to ensure coverage of all shifts. Support from the OH&S team for document retrieval and interview scheduling."
}
